From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] toolchain: check the version stamp without a race

In buildbot mode, every make that reads the top-level Makefile checks
the toolchain's hash stamp while tmp/.build is newer than the stamp.
Each make run from the top level touches tmp/.build, and a stamp that
holds the current hash is left as it is, so the check runs in every one
of these makes. Under -j, world starts several of them at once, such as
those for package/cleanup and target/compile, and each writes the hash
to the same file, tmp/.ver_check, before comparing that file with the
stamp. When one truncates the file while another compares it, the other
sees a different hash: it deletes the toolchain along with the build and
staging directories, and the build fails for want of a compiler.

Compare the hash, which make already holds, with the stamp itself, so
that concurrent checks share no file.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 toolchain/Makefile | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/toolchain/Makefile b/toolchain/Makefile
index 0893c2c..5f39b61 100644
--- a/toolchain/Makefile
+++ b/toolchain/Makefile
@@ -71,11 +71,10 @@ endif
 
 ifdef CONFIG_BUILDBOT
   $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/stamp/.ver_check: $(TMP_DIR)/.build
-	echo $(toolchain_hash) > $(TMP_DIR)/.ver_check
-	cmp -s $(TMP_DIR)/.ver_check $@ || { \
+	[ "$(toolchain_hash)" = "$$(cat $@ 2>/dev/null)" ] || { \
 		rm -rf $(BUILD_DIR) $(STAGING_DIR) $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR) $(BUILD_DIR_TOOLCHAIN); \
 		mkdir -p $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/stamp; \
-		mv $(TMP_DIR)/.ver_check $@; \
+		echo $(toolchain_hash) > $@; \
 	}
 
 $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/info.mk $(STAGING_DIR)/.prepared: $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/stamp/.ver_check
